From a8873dc18d58f3d21229da1af5ccf4f1d8f39ebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonat=C3=A3=20Bolzan=20Loss?= <jonata@jonata.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:21:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] Haiku: V8 platform, Dawn, ANGLE, libsync, pkg-config

V8 gets V8_OS_HAIKU (POSIX, no target OS define, so none of the Linux
signal/trap-handler code) and platform-haiku.cc, carried forward from
the Qt 5 port: image list from get_next_image_info, stack start from
get_thread_info, thread ids and names via find_thread/rename_thread.
Dawn counts Haiku with the BSDs. ANGLE builds no GL or Vulkan backend on
Haiku (no EGL/GLX display; it renders in software). libsync compiles to
ioctls that fail. Chromium's pkg-config wrapper returned nothing on any
platform it did not know, so no system library had flags: Haiku added
there and to the other build scripts that look at sys.platform.
